{
  "pretreatments": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "description": "Knife milling (KM) for substrates with a total solids content higher than 85%. The knife mill occurs inside a milling chamber with mobile milling elements mounted on a central shaft. The knife mills apply forces able to disaggregate solid particles, slice the fibres and typically produce small pieces."
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "description": "Hammer milling (HM) for substrates with a total solids content ranging between 20 and 85%. The hammer mill consists of a rotor with a set of attached hammers that impact the material against a breaker plate, grinding the fibres into long and thin pieces."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "description": "Extrusion (EX) where raw materials are fed into one end of the system and transported along the length of the barrel with a driving screw. The material is subjected to friction heat, mixing, and vigorous shearing upon pressure release at the finishing end."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "description": "Wet shredding followed by hydrodynamic cavitation (SHC). The wet shredder homogenizes fluids and protects downstream cavitator components from damage. The hydrodynamic cavitation reactor uses a stator and rotor assembly to generate cavitation, controlled by the speed of rotation of the rotor."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "description": "Wet sieving using a vibration screening machine (FRITSCH Analysette 3 PRO) to analyze particle size distribution. The specific surface area is calculated based on the particle size distribution, assuming spherical, non-porous particles with a density of 1 kg/l."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "description": "Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM) analysis for qualitative evaluation of morphological changes in substrates before and after mechanical pretreatment. Samples are prepared by placing them onto aluminium SEM specimen stubs with carbon conductive tabs and then coated with gold during metallization phase."
    }
  ]
}
```
